/-!
# A finite type module on a product of qcqs schemes is a quotient of an external tensor product

[Stacks, Tag 0FZ1]: let `R` be a ring and let `X`, `Y` be quasi-compact quasi-separated
`R`-schemes with the resolution property.  Every finite type quasi-coherent
`𝒪_{X ×_R Y}`-module `F` admits a surjection `𝓔 ⊠ 𝓖 ⟶ F` with `𝓔` finite locally free on `X`
and `𝓖` finite locally free on `Y`.  No Noetherian hypothesis is made anywhere.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_pullback_hom_app_unit_eq`: for a quasi-compact quasi-separated
  morphism `h : Z ⟶ T` to a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme with the resolution property,
  a section of a quasi-coherent `𝒪_Z`-module over `h⁻¹ V`, `V` affine, is locally the image of
  `h^*𝓖 ⟶ M` for a finite locally free `𝓖` on `T`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.restrictUnitSliceIso`: over an open `O`, the unit `F ⟶ ι_* ι⁻¹ F` of the
  open immersion `ι : O ⟶ Z` is an isomorphism on the slice site over `O`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_hom_app_eq_smul_restrict_of_qcqs`: one affine piece: a section of
  `F` over `U ×_S V` is locally the image of a morphism `𝓔 ⊠ 𝓖 ⟶ F`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_epi_externalTensorProduct_of_isFiniteType`: the
  statement over an arbitrary base `S` for quasi-compact quasi-separated structure morphisms.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_externalTensorProduct_epi_of_isFiniteType_of_quasiSeparatedSpace`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0FZ1]**, over `Spec R`.

## The argument

The source reduces to [Stacks, Tag 0FZ0] by absolute Noetherian approximation.  This file argues
directly instead, with the resolution property of `X` and of `Y` used on finite type submodules
of direct images, which needs no finiteness of `F` beyond what generation on affines provides.

The product is covered by finitely many affine opens `U ×_S V` (`U ⊆ X`, `V ⊆ Y` affine), and
over each of them `F` is generated by finitely many sections ([Stacks, Tag 01PB]).  Fix one
section `s` of `F` over `U ×_S V`, and write `O = pr₁⁻¹ U`, `ι : O ⟶ X ×_S Y`.

* *The `Y` step.*  `s` is a section of `pr₂_* ι_* ι⁻¹ F` over `V`.  That module is
  quasi-coherent ([Stacks, Tag 01LC]), so `s` lies in a finite type quasi-coherent submodule
  ([Stacks, Tag 01PG]), which is a quotient of a finite locally free `𝓖` by the resolution
  property of `Y`.  The adjoint is a morphism `β : pr₂^* 𝓖 ⟶ ι_* ι⁻¹ F` with `s` locally in its
  image.
* *The `X` step.*  Over `O` the unit `F ⟶ ι_* ι⁻¹ F` is an isomorphism, so `β` restricts to a
  section `t` over `O` of the sheaf Hom `SheafHom(pr₂^* 𝓖, F)`, which is quasi-coherent because
  `pr₂^* 𝓖` is of finite presentation.  The same argument along `pr₁` gives a finite locally
  free `𝓔` on `X` and `ψ : pr₁^* 𝓔 ⟶ SheafHom(pr₂^* 𝓖, F)` with `t` locally in its image.
* *Assembly.*  `ψ` induces `𝓔 ⊠ 𝓖 = pr₁^* 𝓔 ⊗ pr₂^* 𝓖 ⟶ F`, `a ⊗ b ↦ ψ(a)(b)`
  (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.InternalHomModules.tensorHomToModule`), and near every point of
  `U ×_S V` the section `s` is the value of this morphism on a pure tensor.

The finitely many morphisms so obtained are combined into one by
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_factor_externalTensorProduct`, exactly as in the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0FZ0] in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ResolutionsAndBounds/`
`ExternalTensorResolution.lean`, whose section-level epimorphism criterion is reused.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FZ1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FZ1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FZ0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FZ0)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01LC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01LC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PB)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace

universe u

noncomputable section

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable {X Y S : Scheme.{u}}

/-- **One section, made the image of a pullback of a finite locally free module.** Let
`h : Z ⟶ T` be quasi-compact and quasi-separated, with `T` quasi-compact, quasi-separated and
having the resolution property, and let `M` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_Z`-module.  For an affine
open `V ⊆ T` and a section `s` of `M` over `h⁻¹ V` there are a finite locally free `𝒪_T`-module
`𝓖` and a morphism `ψ : h^* 𝓖 ⟶ M` such that near every point of `V` the section `s` is the
value of `ψ` on the image of a section of `𝓖` under the unit of `h^* ⊣ h_*`. -/
theorem exists_pullback_hom_app_unit_eq {Z T : Scheme.{u}} (h : Z ⟶ T) [QuasiCompact h]
    [QuasiSeparated h] [CompactSpace T] [QuasiSeparatedSpace T] [HasResolutionProperty T]
    (M : Z.Modules) [M.IsQuasicoherent] (V : T.affineOpens) (s : Γ(M, h ⁻¹ᵁ V.1)) :
    ∃ (G : T.Modules) (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree (R := T.ringCatSheaf) G)
      (ψ : (Scheme.Modules.pullback h).obj G ⟶ M),
      ∀ y ∈ V.1, ∃ (V' : T.Opens) (hV' : V' ≤ V.1), y ∈ V' ∧ ∃ g : Γ(G, V'),
        ψ.app (h ⁻¹ᵁ V')
            ((((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction h).unit.app G).app V') g) =
          M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h.preimage_mono hV')).op s := by
  obtain ⟨B, hBq, hBf, e, -, hrange⟩ :=
    Stacks.Tag07RMSectionLift.exists_hom_forall_mem_range_pushforward h M
      (fun _ : Unit => V) (fun _ => s)
  obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hrange ()
  obtain ⟨G, hG, π, hπ⟩ := HasResolutionProperty.exists_finiteLocallyFree_quotient B
  refine ⟨G, hG, ((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction h).homEquiv _ _).symm (π ≫ e),
    fun y hy => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨V', hV', hyV', g, hg⟩ := exists_app_eq_of_epi π hπ V.1 w y hy
  refine ⟨V', hV', hyV', g, ?_⟩
  have hadj := (Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction h).homEquiv_unit (X := G) (Y := M)
    (((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction h).homEquiv _ _).symm (π ≫ e))
  rw [Equiv.apply_symm_apply] at hadj
  have h1 := congrArg (fun φ => Scheme.Modules.Hom.app φ V' g) hadj
  simp only [Scheme.Modules.Hom.comp_app, Scheme.Modules.pushforward_map_app] at h1
  refine h1.symm.trans ?_
  change e.app V' (π.app V' g) = _
  rw [hg, app_map_homOfLE e hV' w, hw]
  rfl

/-- A restriction map between two equal opens is bijective. -/
theorem bijective_map_homOfLE_of_eq {Z : Scheme.{u}} (M : Z.Modules) {W₁ W₂ : Z.Opens}
    (h : W₁ ≤ W₂) (heq : W₁ = W₂) : Function.Bijective (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op) := by
  subst heq
  have : (homOfLE h).op = 𝟙 (op W₁) := Subsingleton.elim _ _
  rw [this, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id]
  exact Function.bijective_id

/-- Over an open `O`, the unit `F ⟶ ι_* ι⁻¹ F` of the open immersion `ι : O ⟶ Z` is an
isomorphism of presheaves of modules on the slice site over `O`. -/
def restrictUnitSliceIso {Z : Scheme.{u}} (O : Z.Opens) (F : Z.Modules) :
    (restrFun Z.sheaf.obj O).obj F.val ≅
      (restrFun Z.sheaf.obj O).obj
        ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward O.ι).obj (F.restrict O.ι)).val :=
  have hiso : ∀ W : (Over O)ᵒᵖ, IsIso (((restrFun Z.sheaf.obj O).map
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictAdjunction O.ι).unit.app F).val).app W) := fun W => by
    refine (ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective _).2 ?_
    refine bijective_map_homOfLE_of_eq F (O.ι.image_preimage_le W.unop.left) ?_
    rw [Scheme.Hom.image_preimage_eq_opensRange_inf, Scheme.Opens.opensRange_ι]
    exact inf_eq_right.2 (leOfHom W.unop.hom)
  PresheafOfModules.isoMk (fun W => @asIso _ _ _ _ _ (hiso W))
    (fun _ _ i => ((restrFun Z.sheaf.obj O).map
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictAdjunction O.ι).unit.app F).val).naturality i)

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.InternalHomModules in
/-- Evaluating the restriction of a section of a sheaf Hom is evaluating the section at the
corresponding object of the slice site. -/
theorem evalSection_sheafHomModules_map {Z : Scheme.{u}} (G F : Z.Modules) {W O : Z.Opens}
    (h : W ≤ O) (α : Γ(sheafHomModules G F, O)) (b : Γ(G, W)) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.evalSection Z.sheaf.obj G.val F.val (op W)
        ((sheafHomModules G F).presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op α) b =
      (α.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE h)))).hom b :=
  rfl

/-- The component of `restrFun.map β ≫ (restrictUnitSliceIso O F).inv` at an object of the slice
site over `O` is `β` followed by the inverse of the unit. -/
theorem restrFun_map_comp_inv_app {Z : Scheme.{u}} (O : Z.Opens) {G F : Z.Modules}
    (β : G ⟶ (Scheme.Modules.pushforward O.ι).obj (F.restrict O.ι)) {W : Z.Opens} (h : W ≤ O)
    (b : Γ(G, W)) :
    (((restrFun Z.sheaf.obj O).map β.val ≫ (restrictUnitSliceIso O F).inv).app
        (op (Over.mk (homOfLE h)))).hom b =
      ((restrictUnitSliceIso O F).inv.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE h)))).hom (β.app W b) :=
  rfl

/-- The inverse of `restrictUnitSliceIso` undoes the unit `F ⟶ ι_* ι⁻¹ F` on sections. -/
theorem restrictUnitSliceIso_inv_unit {Z : Scheme.{u}} (O : Z.Opens) (F : Z.Modules)
    {W : Z.Opens} (h : W ≤ O) (v : Γ(F, W)) :
    ((restrictUnitSliceIso O F).inv.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE h)))).hom
        (((Scheme.Modules.restrictAdjunction O.ι).unit.app F).app W v) = v := by
  have hhom : ((restrictUnitSliceIso O F).hom.app (op (Over.mk (homOfLE h)))).hom v =
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictAdjunction O.ι).unit.app F).app W v := rfl
  rw [← hhom]
  have hc := congrArg (fun φ => PresheafOfModules.Hom.app φ (op (Over.mk (homOfLE h))))
    (restrictUnitSliceIso O F).hom_inv_id
  exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom hc v

/-- If `ψ` sends the unit image of `g` to the restriction of `m`, so does the restriction of that
image to any smaller open. -/
private theorem app_map_unit_eq_of_app_unit_eq {Z T : Scheme.{u}} (h : Z ⟶ T) {G : T.Modules}
    {M : Z.Modules} (ψ : (Scheme.Modules.pullback h).obj G ⟶ M) {V' : T.Opens}
    {A W : Z.Opens} (hA : h ⁻¹ᵁ V' ≤ A) (m : Γ(M, A)) (g : Γ(G, V'))
    (hg : ψ.app (h ⁻¹ᵁ V') ((((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction h).unit.app G).app V')
      g) = M.presheaf.map (homOfLE hA).op m) (hW : W ≤ h ⁻¹ᵁ V') :
    ψ.app W ((Scheme.Modules.pullback h).obj G |>.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW).op
        ((((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction h).unit.app G).app V') g)) =
      M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hW.trans hA)).op m := by
  refine (app_map_homOfLE ψ hW _).trans ?_
  rw [hg, map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.InternalHomModules in
/-- **One affine piece of [Stacks, Tag 0FZ1].** Let `X ⟶ S` and `Y ⟶ S` be quasi-compact and
quasi-separated, with `X` and `Y` quasi-compact, quasi-separated and having the resolution
property, and let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_{X ×_S Y}`-module.  For affine opens `U ⊆ X`,
`V ⊆ Y` and a section `s` of `F` over `U ×_S V` there are finite locally free `𝓔` on `X`, `𝓖` on
`Y` and a morphism `φ : 𝓔 ⊠ 𝓖 ⟶ F` such that every multiple `c · s|_{W'}` is, near every point
of `W'`, the image under `φ` of a section.  This is the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_hom_app_eq_smul_restrict` gives in the Noetherian case. -/
theorem exists_hom_app_eq_smul_restrict_of_qcqs (f : X ⟶ S) (g : Y ⟶ S)
    [QuasiCompact f] [QuasiSeparated f] [QuasiCompact g] [QuasiSeparated g]
    [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] [HasResolutionProperty X]
    [CompactSpace Y] [QuasiSeparatedSpace Y] [HasResolutionProperty Y]
    (F : (pullback f g).Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] (U : X.affineOpens) (V : Y.affineOpens)
    (s : Γ(F, pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ V.1)) :
    ∃ (E : X.Modules) (G : Y.Modules)
      (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree (R := X.ringCatSheaf) E)
      (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree (R := Y.ringCatSheaf) G)
      (φ : externalTensorProduct f g E G ⟶ F),
      ∀ (W' : (pullback f g).Opens)
        (hW' : W' ≤ pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ V.1)
        (c : Γ(pullback f g, W')) (p : (pullback f g : Scheme.{u})), p ∈ W' →
        ∃ (W'' : (pullback f g).Opens) (h : W'' ≤ W'), p ∈ W'' ∧
          ∃ u : Γ(externalTensorProduct f g E G, W''),
            φ.app W'' u =
              F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op (c • F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW').op s) := by
  classical
  have : QuasiSeparatedSpace (pullback f g : Scheme.{u}) :=
    quasiSeparatedSpace_of_quasiSeparated (pullback.snd f g)
  have hOc := (pullback.fst f g).isCompact_preimage U.2.isCompact
  have : QuasiCompact (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).ι := quasiCompact_opens_ι hOc
  have hle : (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).ι ''ᵁ
      (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).ι ⁻¹ᵁ (pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ V.1) ≤
        pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.image_preimage_eq_opensRange_inf, Scheme.Opens.opensRange_ι]
  obtain ⟨s', hs'⟩ : ∃ s' : Γ(F.restrict (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).ι,
      (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).ι ⁻¹ᵁ (pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ V.1)),
      s' = F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op s := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨G, hG, β, hβ⟩ := exists_pullback_hom_app_unit_eq (pullback.snd f g)
    ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).ι).obj
      (F.restrict (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).ι)) V s'
  have hPfl : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree (R := (pullback f g).ringCatSheaf)
      ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.snd f g)).obj G) :=
    SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.pullback_scheme _ G hG
  have hPfp : ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.snd f g)).obj G).IsFinitePresentation :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentation_of_isFiniteLocallyFree
      (R := (pullback f g).ringCatSheaf) _
  have : (sheafHomModules ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.snd f g)).obj G) F).IsQuasicoherent :=
    isQuasicoherent_sheafHomModules _ F hPfp
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ : ∃ t : Γ(sheafHomModules ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.snd f g)).obj G) F,
      pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1),
      t = (restrFun (pullback f g).sheaf.obj (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)).map β.val ≫
        (restrictUnitSliceIso (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) F).inv := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨E, hE, ψ, hψ⟩ := exists_pullback_hom_app_unit_eq (pullback.fst f g)
    (sheafHomModules ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.snd f g)).obj G) F) U t
  obtain ⟨φ, hφ⟩ : ∃ φ : externalTensorProduct f g E G ⟶ F, ∀ (W : (pullback f g).Opens)
      (a : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.fst f g)).obj E, W))
      (b : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.snd f g)).obj G, W)),
      φ.app W (Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.toTensorSheafSection
        (pullback f g).toRingedSpace _ _ (op W) (a ⊗ₜ b)) =
        Stacks.SheafOfModules.evalSection (pullback f g).sheaf.obj _ F.val (op W) (ψ.app W a) b :=
    ⟨tensorHomToModule ψ, fun W a b => tensorHomToModule_app_toTensorSheafSection ψ W a b⟩
  refine ⟨E, G, hE, hG, φ, fun W' hW' c p hp => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨U', hU', hpU', x, hx⟩ := hψ _ (hW' hp).1
  obtain ⟨V', hV', hpV', y, hy⟩ := hβ _ (hW' hp).2
  set W'' : (pullback f g).Opens :=
    W' ⊓ pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U' ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ V' with hW''
  have h₀ : W'' ≤ W' := inf_le_left.trans inf_le_left
  have h₁ : W'' ≤ pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U' := inf_le_left.trans inf_le_right
  have h₂ : W'' ≤ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ V' := inf_le_right
  have h₃ : W'' ≤ pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 := h₀.trans hW'
  set a := ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.fst f g)).obj E).presheaf.map (homOfLE h₁).op
    ((((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction (pullback.fst f g)).unit.app E).app U') x)
    with ha
  set b := ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.snd f g)).obj G).presheaf.map (homOfLE h₂).op
    ((((Scheme.Modules.pullbackPushforwardAdjunction (pullback.snd f g)).unit.app G).app V') y)
    with hb
  obtain ⟨τ, hτ⟩ : ∃ τ : Γ(externalTensorProduct f g E G, W''),
      τ = Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.toTensorSheafSection
        (pullback f g).toRingedSpace _ _ (op W'') (a ⊗ₜ b) := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  refine ⟨W'', h₀, ⟨⟨hp, hpU'⟩, hpV'⟩, (pullback f g).presheaf.map (homOfLE h₀).op c • τ, ?_⟩
  rw [Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_smul, hτ, hφ, Scheme.Modules.map_smul,
    map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]
  congr 1
  have hWO : W'' ≤ pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 := h₃.trans inf_le_left
  have hψa : ψ.app W'' a =
      (sheafHomModules ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (pullback.snd f g)).obj G) F).presheaf.map
        (homOfLE hWO).op t := by
    rw [ha, app_map_unit_eq_of_app_unit_eq _ ψ _ t x (hx.trans (by rw [ht])) h₁]
  have hβb : β.app W'' b =
      ((Scheme.Modules.restrictAdjunction (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).ι).unit.app F).app W''
        (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₃).op s) := by
    rw [hb, app_map_unit_eq_of_app_unit_eq _ β _ s' y hy h₂, hs',
      Scheme.Modules.restrictAdjunction_unit_app_app]
    refine Eq.trans ?_ (map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE F h₃
      ((pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1).ι.image_preimage_le W'') s).symm
    change F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (Scheme.Hom.image_mono _ (Scheme.Hom.preimage_mono _
      (h₂.trans ((pullback.snd f g).preimage_mono hV'))))).op
        (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hle).op s) = _
    rw [map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]
  rw [hψa, evalSection_sheafHomModules_map, ht, restrFun_map_comp_inv_app, hβb,
    restrictUnitSliceIso_inv_unit]

/-- **A finite type quasi-coherent module on a fibre product of two quasi-compact
quasi-separated schemes with the resolution property is a quotient of an external tensor product
of finite locally free modules**, over an arbitrary base and for quasi-compact quasi-separated
structure morphisms. -/
theorem exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_epi_externalTensorProduct_of_isFiniteType (f : X ⟶ S)
    (g : Y ⟶ S) [QuasiCompact f] [QuasiSeparated f] [QuasiCompact g] [QuasiSeparated g]
    [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] [HasResolutionProperty X]
    [CompactSpace Y] [QuasiSeparatedSpace Y] [HasResolutionProperty Y]
    (F : (pullback f g).Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [F.IsFiniteType] :
    ∃ (E : X.Modules) (G : Y.Modules)
      (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree (R := X.ringCatSheaf) E)
      (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree (R := Y.ringCatSheaf) G)
      (q : externalTensorProduct f g E G ⟶ F), Epi q := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨m, U, V, haff, hcov⟩ := exists_finite_affine_product_cover f g
  have hgen : ∀ i : Fin m, ∃ (k : ℕ)
      (s : Fin k → Γ(F, pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ (U i).1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ (V i).1)),
      ∀ (W₁ : (pullback f g).Opens)
        (h₁ : W₁ ≤ pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ (U i).1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ (V i).1)
        (t : Γ(F, W₁)) (p : (pullback f g : Scheme.{u})), p ∈ W₁ →
        ∃ (W₂ : (pullback f g).Opens) (h₂ : W₂ ≤ W₁)
          (h₃ : W₂ ≤ pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ (U i).1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ (V i).1), p ∈ W₂ ∧
          ∃ c : Fin k → Γ(pullback f g, W₂),
            F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₂).op t =
              ∑ j, c j • F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₃).op (s j) := by
    intro i
    have : Module.Finite Γ(pullback f g, pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ (U i).1 ⊓
        pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ (V i).1)
        Γ(F, pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ (U i).1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ (V i).1) :=
      Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentFinite.finite_sections F (haff i)
    obtain ⟨k, s, hs⟩ := Module.Finite.exists_fin (R := Γ(pullback f g,
      pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ (U i).1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ (V i).1))
      (M := Γ(F, pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ (U i).1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ (V i).1))
    exact ⟨k, s, fun W₁ h₁ t p hp =>
      exists_sum_smul_sections_of_span_eq_top F (haff i) s hs h₁ t p hp⟩
  choose k s hs using hgen
  choose Em Gm hEm hGm φ hφ using fun (i : Fin m) (j : Fin (k i)) =>
    exists_hom_app_eq_smul_restrict_of_qcqs f g F (U i) (V i) (s i j)
  obtain ⟨E', G', hE', hG', θ, hfac⟩ := exists_factor_externalTensorProduct f g F
    (Λ := Σ i : Fin m, Fin (k i)) (fun l => Em l.1 l.2) (fun l => Gm l.1 l.2)
    (fun l => hEm l.1 l.2) (fun l => hGm l.1 l.2) (fun l => φ l.1 l.2)
  choose ι hι using hfac
  refine ⟨E', G', hE', hG', θ, epi_of_exists_app_eq θ fun W t p hp => ?_⟩
  have hpT : p ∈ ⨆ i, pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ (U i).1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ (V i).1 := by
    rw [hcov]
    trivial
  obtain ⟨i, hpi⟩ := Opens.mem_iSup.mp hpT
  obtain ⟨W₂, h₂, h₃, hpW₂, c, hc⟩ :=
    hs i (W ⊓ (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ (U i).1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ (V i).1)) inf_le_right
      (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (inf_le_left :
        W ⊓ (pullback.fst f g ⁻¹ᵁ (U i).1 ⊓ pullback.snd f g ⁻¹ᵁ (V i).1) ≤ W)).op t)
      p ⟨hp, hpi⟩
  choose Wl hWl hpWl u hu using fun j => hφ i j W₂ h₃ (c j) p hpW₂
  obtain ⟨Wc, hpWc, hWcW₂, hWcl⟩ := exists_opens_mem_le_of_fin Wl hpWl W₂ hpW₂
  refine ⟨Wc, hWcW₂.trans (h₂.trans inf_le_left), hpWc,
    ∑ j, (ι ⟨i, j⟩).app Wc
      ((externalTensorProduct f g (Em i j) (Gm i j)).presheaf.map
        (homOfLE (hWcl j)).op (u j)), ?_⟩
  refine Eq.trans (map_sum (θ.app Wc).hom _ Finset.univ) ?_
  have hterm : ∀ j : Fin (k i),
      θ.app Wc ((ι ⟨i, j⟩).app Wc
          ((externalTensorProduct f g (Em i j) (Gm i j)).presheaf.map
            (homOfLE (hWcl j)).op (u j)))
        = F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWcW₂).op
            (c j • F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₃).op (s i j)) := by
    intro j
    have h4 : θ.app Wc ((ι ⟨i, j⟩).app Wc
        ((externalTensorProduct f g (Em i j) (Gm i j)).presheaf.map
          (homOfLE (hWcl j)).op (u j)))
        = (φ i j).app Wc ((externalTensorProduct f g (Em i j) (Gm i j)).presheaf.map
          (homOfLE (hWcl j)).op (u j)) :=
      congrArg (fun χ => Scheme.Modules.Hom.app χ Wc
        ((externalTensorProduct f g (Em i j) (Gm i j)).presheaf.map
          (homOfLE (hWcl j)).op (u j))) (hι ⟨i, j⟩)
    rw [h4, app_map_homOfLE (φ i j) (hWcl j), hu j, map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => hterm j, ← map_sum (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWcW₂).op).hom,
    ← hc, map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE, map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]

/-- Let `R` be a ring and let `X`, `Y` be quasi-compact and quasi-separated schemes over `R`
having the resolution property.  For every finite type quasi-coherent `𝒪_{X ×_R Y}`-module `F`
there is a surjection `𝓔 ⊠ 𝓖 ⟶ F` with `𝓔` a finite locally free `𝒪_X`-module and `𝓖` a finite
locally free `𝒪_Y`-module. -/
@[stacks 0FZ1]
theorem exists_externalTensorProduct_epi_of_isFiniteType_of_quasiSeparatedSpace
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) (g : Y ⟶ Spec (.of R))
    [CompactSpace X] [QuasiSeparatedSpace X] [CompactSpace Y] [QuasiSeparatedSpace Y]
    [HasResolutionProperty X] [HasResolutionProperty Y]
    (F : (pullback f g).Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent] [F.IsFiniteType] :
    ∃ (E : X.Modules) (G : Y.Modules)
      (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree (R := X.ringCatSheaf) E)
      (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree (R := Y.ringCatSheaf) G)
      (q : externalTensorProduct f g E G ⟶ F), Epi q :=
  exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_epi_externalTensorProduct_of_isFiniteType f g F

end AlgebraicGeometry
